>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `GEN_SIMP_TAC`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC : simpExtLib.simp_mode ->
  simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> tactic
simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST : TraverseExt.child_first_policy ->
  simpExtLib.simp_mode -> simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Simplifies a goal, then applies an extension simpset's solvers and loopers.

`GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe} ss ths` processes directives, simplifies with the
selected assumptions, tries final solvers in order (safe if `safe`, unsafe
otherwise), then applies the first successful looper and repeats on its
subgoals. Unsafe solvers still handle conditional rewrite premises in safe
mode. Final solver proofs must have the goal as conclusion and only goal
assumptions as hypotheses. `limit n ss` allows at most `n` successful looper
applications in the invocation.

Supplied rules are bound once per invocation, sharing their actual bounded
controls across branches, recursive passes and solver `recurse` calls.
Solver contexts contain untagged theorems, not bounded-marker statements.
Local directive replay preserves all installed controls, not just supplied
rules. `NoAsms` and `IgnAsm` select assumptions again for each pass, including
when nested under requirement or bounded wrappers. Bounds qualify directives;
they do not turn them into rewrite rules.

The child-first variant explicitly selects `TraverseExt` traversal. Both
variants require extension sets constructed from, for example,
`simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss`. Conversions do not run final
solvers or loopers.

### Failure

May diverge if a looper succeeds without progress and no limit is set.
Invalid directives or failed requirement checks can raise `HOL_ERR`.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_safe_solver
     (simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver ("arith", DECIDE_TAC))
     (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss);
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = true} ss [] ([], “x < x + 1”) c;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST
     (TraverseExt.charge_only (fn () => ())) {safe = false}
     ss [markerLib.NoAsms] ([], “x < x + 1”) c;
```

